<p>
I have long struggled with predicting when peace will occur. Actually, I&rsquo;m
struggling with predicting anything relating to war, but let&rsquo;s focus on when peace arrives for now. There are two such
questions in the current ACX 2026 competition:
</p>



<ul class="org-ul">
<li>Will there be a cease-fire in Ukraine in 2026?</li>
<li>Will there be a cease-fire in Sudan in 2026?</li>
</ul>



<p>
When I entered my forecast for these questions, I did it based on Laplace&rsquo;s rule
of succession, i.e. as a function of their duration only. This is sort of
justified if war durations are heavy-tailed, which would mean that the longer
they go on for, the less likely it is that peace comes soon. But I don&rsquo;t
know if that is true.
